---
title: Pecan pie
servings: 10
yield: one 9-inch pie
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, holiday, fall, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour 30 minutes
source: Pecan Pie by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/pecan-pie-recipe
---

> Use one disc of the crust from Buttery pie crust (baking/pies-and-tarts), in a pie pan at least 2 inches deep.

== Crust ==

Heat the oven to 400°F. Roll the dough to a 13-inch round, fit it into a greased #9-inch pie pan{}, trim and crimp. Chill ~{10%minutes}.

Line it with foil, fill with #pie weights{} and bake ~{10%minutes}. Lift out the weights and foil and lower the oven to 325°F.

== Filling ==

Spread the @pecans{57%g}(chopped) on a #baking sheet{}, sprinkle with a little of the @table salt{1/2%tsp} and toast ~{10%minutes} to 15 minutes, until fragrant. Let them cool and raise the oven to 375°F.

Beat the @eggs{3}, @dark corn syrup{163%g}, @light corn syrup{163%g}, @granulated sugar{50%g}, @unsalted butter{113%g}(melted), @vanilla extract{1%tsp} and the rest of the salt in a #medium bowl{}.

Stir in the toasted pecans and pour into the shell. Lay the @pecans{113%g}(halves) over the top.

Bake ~{45%minutes}, until puffed and fairly set in the middle. Cool completely on a #wire rack{}; the centre sinks as it cools.

> Keep it in the fridge once cool. Warm slices briefly if you like.
